    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330-a2">

                <pb facs="0585" n="523" xml:id="pg523"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2, No. 290.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Turner to Mr.
                            Johnson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-01-05"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 5,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have had the honor to receive your
                    dispatch of even date. It announces your appointment by His Excellency the
                    Acting President to be Secretary of State; and extends to me an invitation to be
                    present on the occasion of the inauguration of Hons. A. W. Gardner and D. B.
                    Warner, into the Presidency and Vice-Presidency of the republic.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept my congratulations upon your attainment to the distinguished
                    post of Secretary of State. The invitation which you have extended to me is
                    accepted; and I hope to have the honor to be present on the occasion referred
                    to.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, Mr. Secretary, with considerations of high esteem, your
                    obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. MILTON TURNER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
